    "Trade economics (notionals $50mm, strikes, fixed rates) are REPRESENTATIVE placeholders \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the design doc specifies instrument types, not terms. Adjust per real trade tickets.",
    "default_valuation_date = 2026-05-29 is the latest Pensford SOFR forward-curve snapshot (the binding curve input). Override with --valuation-date.",
    "Swaptions/cap strikes set to null => priced ATM-forward. Swaption/cap vol = flat normal (Bachelier) level from configs/pricer/pricer_config.json (MOVE-anchored).",
    "Bonds #15-19: terms (coupon/maturity/CUSIP) from configs/marketdata/bonds. Discounted on SOFR + issuer credit spread (config fallback, since free CDS is unusable). Bonds #20-21 are the on-the-run 2Y/10Y USTs (from TreasuryDirect), discounted on the bootstrapped UST par curve. Face amounts $50mm placeholders.",
    "Equity options #7-14: strikes/expiries are REPRESENTATIVE (expiries chosen on real chain dates; strikes round near recovered spot). Spot + dividend yield recovered from the chain via put-call parity; per-leg IV from the chain (skew-aware). These value at the 2026-06-17 chain snapshot \u00e2\u20ac\u201d run equities with --valuation-date 2026-06-17. Contract counts are placeholders.",
    "Cash equity #1-6: signed share quantities are REPRESENTATIVE (~$50mm gross each). Marked at the daily close on/before the valuation date; SMH (#6) is a short. These have full daily history so value at the 2026-05-29 default like rates/bonds.",
    "Credit/CDS #28-30: $50mm notionals (placeholders). 5Y par spreads from DTCC (single-name SEC path / index CFTC path), filtered to the 5Y bucket; flat hazard calibrated to par under IsdaCdsEngine. ORCL/META buy protection (hedge bonds #17/#18); CDX.NA.IG sell protection. Standard 100bp IG running coupon, 40% recovery.",
    "FX #26-27: REPRESENTATIVE terms. #26 USD/TWD 5Y CCS modelled fixed-for-fixed with notional exchange (seasoned: started 2025-05-29 at contract FX 30.00, matures 2030-05-29) - LONG_USD = receive USD / pay TWD, hedging the long-TWD TSM-ADR (#2); gains as TWD weakened to ~31.4. #27 USD/JPY 3M forward, buy USD (carry), struck at-market when rolled (2026-10-06: 156.94, see roll_history). Options #9/#11/#12/#14 were likewise rolled on expiry to the same tenor and moneyness."
